  "excluded_families": {
    "graph_neural_network": "The genotype is a fixed-length vector of five genes, not a graph. Every architecture here has the same topology \u2014 a stack of identical blocks \u2014 so a GCN would receive the same graph 1,099 times with only node features differing, which is a multilayer perceptron with extra steps. Applicable the moment the space admits varying topology: skip connections, branching, or per-layer heterogeneity.",
